.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt KEXTLOAD 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm kextload
.Nd load kernel extensions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl qv
.Op Fl b Ar bundle_id ...
.Op Ar kext ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads the kernel extensions given by path
.Pq Ar kext
or by identifier
.Pq Fl b Ar bundle_id ,
through IOKit's kext functions.
They and the extensions they depend on are linked for the running kernel
and started. Identifiers and dependencies are looked up in
.Pa /System/Library/Extensions
and
.Pa /Library/Extensions .
An extension already loaded is left as it is, and that is not an error.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl b Ar bundle_id
Load the extension with this identifier; it may be repeated.
.It Fl q
Accepted for compatibility; only errors are printed anyway.
.It Fl v
Print the kernel's warnings and progress too.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kextstat 8 ,
.Xr kextunload 8
